tr><tr><td><b>Accreditation</b></td><td>NABSS member; International Schools Partnership group</td></tr><tr><td><b>Results</b></td><td>2026 IGCSE 74% grades 4–9 (school post, unverified)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Best-placed areas</b></td><td>San Pedro, Benahavís, Guadalmina, El Campanario</td></tr><tr><td><b>Location</b></td><td>Coordinates on the Good Schools Guide profile</td></tr></table><p><a href="https://www.goodschoolsguide.co.uk/international/profile/laude-san-pedro-international-college">Source: https://www.goodschoolsguide.co.uk/international/profile/laude-san-pedro-international-college</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-4.9920468,36.486704,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>#7 Queens British Grammar School</name><styleUrl>#school</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Key result</b></td><td>No results published</td></tr><tr><td><b>Area</b></td><td>Costa Galera, Estepona</td></tr><tr><td><b>Curriculum</b></td><td>British (IGCSE, A Levels)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Ages</b></td><td>3–18</td></tr><tr><td><b>Fees</b></td><td>€7,686–€18,606 (2026/27)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Accreditation</b></td><td>Not verified</td></tr><tr><td><b>Results</b></td><td>Not published</td></tr><tr><td><b>Best-placed areas</b></td><td>Estepona town, Casares</td></tr><tr><td><b>Location</b></td><td>APPROXIMATE: School not in OpenStreetMap; pin at Costa Galera, Estepona</td></tr></table><p><a href="https://longtermspain.com/moving-to/estepona/schools">Source: https://longtermspain.com/moving-to/estepona/schools</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-5.2033095,36.3931356,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>#8 Mayfair School</name><styleUrl>#school</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Key result</b></td><td>No results published</td></tr><tr><td><b>Website</b></td><td>https://mayfairschool.es/</td></tr><tr><td><b>Area</b></td><td>Atalaya Park, Estepona</td></tr><tr><td><b>Curriculum</b></td><td>British (Cambridge IGCSE, A Levels)</td></tr><tr><td><b>Ages</b></td><td>3–18</td></tr><tr><td><b>Fees</b></td><td>On request</td></tr><tr><td><b>Accreditation</b></td><td>Not verified</td></tr><tr><td><b>Results</b></td><td>Not published</td></tr><tr><td><b>Best-placed areas</b></td><td>New Golden Mile, El Campanario</td></tr><tr><td><b>Location</b></td><td>OpenStreetMap: &#x27;Mayfair Academy&#x27;, Atalaya Park</td></tr></table><p><a href="https://longtermspain.com/moving-to/estepona/schools">Source: https://longtermspain.com/moving-to/estepona/schools</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-5.0112202,36.4645421,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Hotspots (indicative outlines)</name><Placemark><name>#1 Estepona, incl. New Golden Mile and El Campanario</name><styleUrl>#z-growth</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Status</b></td><td>Growth</td></tr><tr><td><b>Prices</b></td><td>€5,021/m² · +17.1% y/y</td></tr></table><p>Fastest growth on the coast (+17.1%), still about 16% cheaper per m² than Marbella. New builds are about 25% of sales here, against 11% in Marbella. Last frontline beach estate (Sierra Blanca by the Sea), port concession tender (447 berths, €10M+), 2029–2030 deliveries such as Kalifornia and El Campanario phase III. (Outline is indicative, not an official boundary.)</p>]]></description><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>-5.208,36.4,0 -5.17,36.41,0 -5.14,36.422,0 -5.095,36.44,0 -5.06,36.455,0 -5.025,36.466,0 -5.005,36.47,0 -5.005,36.505,0 -5.06,36.5,0 -5.12,36.48,0 -5.18,36.46,0 -5.215,36.435,0 -5.208,36.4,0</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>#2 Marbella East: Las Chapas, Elviria, Río Real, Los Monteros</name><styleUrl>#z-growth</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Status</b></td><td>Growth</td></tr><tr><td><b>Prices</b></td><td>Marbella €5,967/m² · +3.2% y/y (whole municipality)</td></tr></table><p>The biggest hotel-resort wave on the coast: Four Seasons Río Real (~€700M, first deliveries 2029), Las Dunas beachfront resort (€350M+, ~170 branded homes, dune regeneration), Waldorf Astoria at Higuerón Marbella Golf Resort, plus Incosol and Kimpton. EIC on the doorstep. (Outline is indicative, not an official boundary.)</p>]]></description><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>-4.862,36.503,0 -4.83,36.501,0 -4.8,36.494,0 -4.77,36.49,0 -4.736,36.478,0 -4.732,36.52,0 -4.77,36.545,0 -4.83,36.545,0 -4.862,36.535,0 -4.862,36.503,0</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>#3 Benahavís</name><styleUrl>#z-growth</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Status</b></td><td>Growth</td></tr><tr><td><b>Prices</b></td><td>€5,602/m² · +6.5% y/y</td></tr></table><p>€5,602/m², +6.5% asking, but registered sale prices rose 19.6% in H1 2026. Engel &amp; Völkers puts houses in Marbella Club Golf Resort at +12% y/y. Close to Aloha College. (Outline is indicative, not an official boundary.)</p>]]></description><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>-5.065,36.505,0 -5.01,36.508,0 -4.985,36.512,0 -4.975,36.535,0 -5.0,36.555,0 -5.055,36.552,0 -5.075,36.535,0 -5.065,36.505,0</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>#4 Golden Mile, Nagüeles, Sierra Blanca</name><styleUrl>#z-blue</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Status</b></td><td>Blue chip</td></tr><tr><td><b>Prices</b></td><td>Marbella €5,967/m² · +3.2% y/y</td></tr></table><p>Europe&#x27;s densest branded-residence cluster (Armani, Dolce&amp;Gabbana, Bentley, Karl Lagerfeld). Knight Frank puts top-end Marbella at US$1,600–2,700/sq ft, on par with Madrid. Scarce land, so it holds value but grows slower (+3.2%). (Outline is indicative, not an official boundary.)</p>]]></description><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>-4.945,36.49,0 -4.925,36.498,0 -4.9,36.505,0 -4.898,36.53,0 -4.93,36.535,0 -4.945,36.52,0 -4.945,36.49,0</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>#5 Marbella centre and La Bajadilla</name><styleUrl>#z-upgrade</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Status</b></td><td>Upgrade</td></tr><tr><td><b>Prices</b></td><td>Port: 268 → ~750 berths</td></tr></table><p>La Bajadilla port grows from 268 to about 750 berths (yachts up to 70 m) with €200M+ investment, 40-year concession from 1 Jan 2027. New general plan (PGOM) approved Sept 2026. (Outline is indicative, not an official boundary.)</p>]]></description><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>-4.898,36.505,0 -4.88,36.507,0 -4.862,36.506,0 -4.862,36.528,0 -4.898,36.53,0 -4.898,36.505,0</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>#6 Casares, Manilva, Sotogrande</name><styleUrl>#z-growth</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Status</b></td><td>Value</td></tr><tr><td><b>Prices</b></td><td>Manilva €3,043/m² · +11.3% y/y</td></tr></table><p>Cheapest coastal entry (Manilva €3,043/m², +11.3%) with frontline land still available: Nubay, St. Regis at Finca Cortesín (2029), Acciona&#x27;s Villas of Sotogrande. About 80 min from Málaga airport. (Outline is indicative, not an official boundary.)</p>]]></description><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>-5.345,36.27,0 -5.272,36.278,0 -5.25,36.315,0 -5.228,36.338,0 -5.215,36.355,0 -5.205,36.385,0 -5.208,36.4,0 -5.215,36.435,0 -5.29,36.42,0 -5.33,36.33,0 -5.36,36.3,0 -5.345,36.27,0</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>#7 Mijas Costa: Calahonda, La Cala</name><styleUrl>#z-upgrade</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Status</b></td><td>Optionality</td></tr><tr><td><b>Prices</b></td><td>Mijas €3,717/m² · +8.5% y/y</td></tr></table><p>€3,717/m², +8.5%. Gated sea-view villas from €1.65M and big-terrace penthouses from €1.465M. Biggest winner if the coastal train reaches Marbella, but that is long-dated. (Outline is indicative, not an official boundary.)</p>]]></description><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>-4.736,36.478,0 -4.712,36.483,0 -4.69,36.49,0 -4.662,36.505,0 -4.64,36.522,0 -4.63,36.575,0 -4.7,36.575,0 -4.732,36.52,0 -4.736,36.478,0</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Nueva Andalucía &#x27;Golf Valley&#x27;</name><styleUrl>#z-neutral</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Status</b></td><td>Area of interest</td></tr></table><p>Golf-course belt behind Puerto Banús (Aloha, Las Brisas, Los Naranjos clubs). Home to Aloha College and the Ocho de Oro project. Shown for orientation; not one of the ranked hotspots on the research Page. (Outline is indicative, not an official boundary.)</p>]]></description><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>-4.985,36.498,0 -4.955,36.497,0 -4.94,36.51,0 -4.95,36.528,0 -4.985,36.528,0 -4.985,36.498,0</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark><Placemark><name>Marbella Old Town (Casco Antiguo)</name><styleUrl>#z-heritage</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Status</b></td><td>Landmark</td></tr><tr><td><b>Prices</b></td><td>Plaza de los Naranjos</td></tr></table><p>Marbella&#x27;s historic quarter: narrow whitewashed lanes around Plaza de los Naranjos, the Church of the Incarnation and the remains of the Moorish castle walls, full of tapas bars, boutiques and flower-lined streets. A short walk from the Marbella marina and the La Bajadilla port expansion. Outline is indicative. (Outline is indicative, not an official boundary.)</p>]]></description><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>-4.8893,36.5086,0 -4.884,36.5084,0 -4.881,36.5092,0 -4.8803,36.5112,0 -4.8828,36.5127,0 -4.8872,36.5126,0 -4.8896,36.511,0 -4.8893,36.5086,0</coordinates></LinearRing></outerBoundaryIs></Polygon></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Marinas, catalysts &amp; train study</name><Placemark><name>La Bajadilla port expansion</name><styleUrl>#poi</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Kind</b></td><td>Catalyst</td></tr><tr><td><b>Status</b></td><td>Signed (Nov 2026)</td></tr></table><p>Concession contract formalised Nov 2026; operator takes over 1 Jan 2027 for 40 years. Grows from 268 to about 750 berths (yachts up to 70 m), €200M+ investment.</p><p><a href="https://www.europapress.es/andalucia/puertos-del-estado-01056/noticia-formalizado-contrato-concesion-ampliacion-puerto-bajadilla-marbella-malaga-20261110185327.html">Source: https://www.europapress.es/andalucia/puertos-del-estado-01056/noticia-formalizado-contrato-concesion-ampliacion-puerto-bajadilla-marbella-malaga-20261110185327.html</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-4.8742239,36.5068103,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Estepona port concession</name><styleUrl>#poi</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Kind</b></td><td>Catalyst</td></tr><tr><td><b>Status</b></td><td>Tender (2026–27)</td></tr></table><p>30-year concession tendered Feb 2026: 447 berths, €10M minimum investment, refurbishment only. 11 bids received.</p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-5.157274,36.4145944,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Puerto Banús</name><styleUrl>#poi</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Kind</b></td><td>Marina</td></tr></table><p>Marbella&#x27;s best-known luxury marina. Shown as a landmark; not analysed on the research Page.</p><p><a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=36.487587&amp;mlon=-4.9537861#map=16/36.4876/-4.9538">Source: https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=36.487587&amp;mlon=-4.9537861#map=16/36.4876/-4.9538</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-4.9537861,36.487587,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Marbella marina (Puerto Deportivo Virgen del Carmen)</name><styleUrl>#poi</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Kind</b></td><td>Marina</td></tr></table><p>Town-centre marina. Shown as a landmark.</p><p><a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=36.5057403&amp;mlon=-4.8889798#map=16/36.5057/-4.8890">Source: https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=36.5057403&amp;mlon=-4.8889798#map=16/36.5057/-4.8890</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-4.8889798,36.5057403,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Puerto de la Duquesa</name><styleUrl>#poi</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Kind</b></td><td>Marina</td></tr></table><p>Marina at La Duquesa, Manilva, next to the Nubay project. Shown as a landmark.</p><p><a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=36.3549064&amp;mlon=-5.2295179#map=16/36.3549/-5.2295">Source: https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=36.3549064&amp;mlon=-5.2295179#map=16/36.3549/-5.2295</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-5.2295179,36.3549064,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Puerto Sotogrande</name><styleUrl>#poi</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Kind</b></td><td>Marina</td></tr></table><p>Sotogrande marina. Shown as a landmark.</p><p><a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=36.2869816&amp;mlon=-5.2785173#map=16/36.2870/-5.2785">Source: https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=36.2869816&amp;mlon=-5.2785173#map=16/36.2870/-5.2785</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-5.2785173,36.2869816,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Finca Cortesín</name><styleUrl>#poi</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Kind</b></td><td>Golf resort</td></tr></table><p>Golf and hotel resort in Casares; home of the St. Regis Residences (2029 phase) and next to Casares del Sol.</p><p><a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=36.3964579&amp;mlon=-5.2238636#map=16/36.3965/-5.2239">Source: https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=36.3964579&amp;mlon=-5.2238636#map=16/36.3965/-5.2239</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-5.2238636,36.3964579,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>La Zagaleta</name><styleUrl>#poi</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Kind</b></td><td>Prime estate</td></tr></table><p>Gated estate in Benahavís, referenced on the Page as a neighbour of the Benahavís villa-residences.</p><p><a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=36.5396914&amp;mlon=-5.0196147#map=15/36.5397/-5.0196">Source: https://www.openstreetmap.org/?mlat=36.5396914&amp;mlon=-5.0196147#map=15/36.5397/-5.0196</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-5.0196147,36.5396914,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Plaza de los Naranjos (Marbella Old Town)</name><styleUrl>#poi</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Kind</b></td><td>Old town</td></tr><tr><td><b>Status</b></td><td>Historic centre</td></tr></table><p>Heart of Marbella&#x27;s old town: orange-tree square with the town hall, surrounded by the Casco Antiguo&#x27;s whitewashed lanes and tapas bars.</p><p><a href="https://turismo.marbella.es/">Source: https://turismo.marbella.es/</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-4.884986,36.5102335,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Estepona Old Town (Plaza de las Flores)</name><styleUrl>#poi</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Kind</b></td><td>Old town</td></tr><tr><td><b>Status</b></td><td>Historic centre</td></tr></table><p>Estepona&#x27;s &#x27;Garden of the Costa del Sol&#x27;: flower-pot lined white streets around Plaza de las Flores, with murals, the Orchidarium and the beachfront promenade nearby.</p><p><a href="https://turismo.estepona.es/">Source: https://turismo.estepona.es/</a></p>]]></description><Point><coordinates>-5.145475,36.4257342,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Coastal train corridor (indicative)</name><styleUrl>#train</styleUrl><description><![CDATA[<table><tr><td><b>Status</b></td><td>Study due 2 Apr 2027</td></tr></table><p>Feasibility study by WSP/APIA now due 2 April 2027. The government calls Fuengirola–Marbella the priority and likely viable, possibly underground. No construction date; the 2022 study rated all options unviable. Upside, not a base case. The line on the map is schemati